aquinas-evil-objection.logic.r1: argue/equivocates: P2 (S2): "infinite" is taken as God's own goodness is unlimited in degree or perfection, which does not imply that goodness occupies everything in P2 and as one of two contraries is unbounded in extent, filling everything and leaving no room for its opposite where infinite_good is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C1 (S3) does not follow (aquinas-evil-objection.logic.r1.sense1)
aquinas-evil-objection.logic.r1: argue/countermodel: C1 (S3): evil = T, god_exists = T, infinite_good = F, infinite_good_2 = T
